  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% acc, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (config_010, 20.8% acc), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether the profile setting (single vs. multi) matters for RNA, which is a fundamental architectural choice affecting all downstream configurations. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile + avgpool aggregation with the same PCA encoder as config_001, isolating the effect of profile setting while keeping the encoder fixed. If multiprofile improves performance, it validates a design axis that applies universally across encoders and fusion strategies; if it does not, we can rule out that axis and focus budget on encoder choice (scvi, scgpt) or multimodal fusion. This is the most informative single-variable extension of our best result and the best use of the next experiment under a tight budget."
}

